    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "500f6eb1_f06c388a",
        "filename": "ssh/certs.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 6190
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-28T18:20:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right - it is needed if you want to parse the values of Extensions which are (currently) always empty.  Made a corresponding change in the (renamed) parseTuples function - see:\nlength :\u003d binary.BigEndian.Uint32(rest)\nand the following check for length being 0.\n\nI also added a check to verify that the value of bytes[0-3] is the same as that of [4-7] plus 4, and fail with an error if it is not the case (to flag certificates generated with the previous versions of crypto/ssh, or corrupted):\n\n0 - 3:          len(s)+4\n4 - 7:          len(s)\n8 - \u003clen(s)+8\u003e: bytes of s",
      "parentUuid": "f00b02a7_edd22186",
      "revId": "3d1897b2e360065eec7489836712ae27b75dad90",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
