    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "500f6eb1_b357ea5b",
        "filename": "ssh/certs_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 162,
      "author": {
        "id": 6190
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-28T18:20:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that was not very user-friendly.\n\nI have since changed it to a sequence of append calls - I think it shows more clearly how the byte slice is composed and make it easier for others to understand and change than just a dump of characters:\n\n\tb :\u003d []byte{}\n\tfor _, key :\u003d range keys {\n\t\tb \u003d appendInt(b, len(key))\n\t\tb \u003d append(b, []byte(key)...)\n\t\tb \u003d appendInt(b, len(opts[key])+4)\n\t\tb \u003d appendInt(b, len(opts[key]))\n\t\tb \u003d append(b, []byte(opts[key])...)\n\t}\n\nYou also don\u0027t need to change this code composing the byte array if for example you decide to change the values of the options for any reason (or add/remove some pairs).",
      "parentUuid": "f00b02a7_cdd75d74",
      "revId": "3d1897b2e360065eec7489836712ae27b75dad90",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
